10. Bessel Functions of Fractional Order
Mathematical Properties
10.1. Spherical Bessel Functions
Definitions
Differential Equation
10.1.1
2^{n}w^{\prime}+2\pi w^{\prime}+[z^{3}-n(n+1)]w=0 (n=0,\pm 1,\pm2,\ldots)
Particular solutions are the Spherical Bessel functions of the first kind
j_n(z)=\sqrt{2\pi/2}J_{n+1}(z), the Spherical Bessel functions of the second kind
y_n(z)=\sqrt{3\pi/2}Y_{n+1}(z), and the Spherical Bessel functions of the third kind
h_n(1)=j_n(z)+iy_n(z)=\sqrt{2\pi/2}H_{n+1}^{(1)}(z), h_n(2)=j_n(z)-iy_n(z)=\sqrt{1\pi/2}H_{n+1}^{(2)}(z).
The pairs j_n(z), y_n(z) and h_n(1)(z), h_n(2) are linearly independent solutions for every n. For general properties see the remarks after 9.1.1.
According Series (Sep 9.1.2, 9.1.10)
10.1.2
j_n(z)=\frac{z^{3}}{1.3\cdot5\ldots(2n+1)}\left\{1-\frac{\tfrac12}{1!(2n+3)}{1!(2n+3)}\right.\qquad\